  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_006: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, acc=0.725) has only been tested with imagenet_vit_l as the image encoder. All top-performing multimodal configs use this specific encoder, leaving the image encoder architecture as an unexplored critical design dimension in the high-performing regime. Config_038 makes a single-variable change (imagenet_vit_l → resnet50) from config_006, cleanly isolating the effect of image encoder choice. If resnet50 performs comparably, the image modality contribution is robust to architecture and we can focus optimization on other axes; if it drops significantly, it confirms imagenet_vit_l is essential and the gap informs how much the image representation contributes. This is the best use of the next experiment because it tests the least-resolved design choice in the current best-performing region, provides actionable guidance for practical deployment (lighter encoder), and is a controlled single-variable comparison rather than a multi-factor change."
